abstract: >
  RISE is a public knowledge base introducing Research Information
  Systems Engineering — the design and study of information systems
  that produce scholarly knowledge, with a focus on agentic research
  pipelines. It maintains three curated catalogs: (i) an
  academic-papers database with structured notes, (ii) a projects
  database evaluating agentic research systems against a standard
  rubric, and (iii) a skills database of reusable Markdown skill
  files curated from open agentic-research projects. The site also
  ships a Get-started guide for researchers adopting coding agents.
